UDP FILE RECEIVER (Server) — save as udp_server.py

import socket

server = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)
server.bind(("localhost", 7000))
print("Server ready to receive file...")

# File name receive
data, addr = server.recvfrom(1024)
filename = data.decode()
print("Receiving file:", filename)

file = open("received_" + filename, "wb")

while True:
    data, addr = server.recvfrom(1024)
    if data == b"EOF":
        break
    file.write(data)

file.close()
print("File received successfully.")
server.close()


UDP FILE SENDER (Client) — save as udp_client.py

import socket

client = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)

filename = input("Enter filename to send: ")
client.sendto(filename.encode(), ("localhost", 7000))

file = open(filename, "rb")
data = file.read(1024)

while data:
    client.sendto(data, ("localhost", 7000))
    data = file.read(1024)

file.close()
client.sendto(b"EOF", ("localhost", 7000))
print("File sent successfully.")
client.close()






How to Run 

Place both files in the same folder.

Prepare any file:

script.py

notes.txt

song.mp3

video.mp4

ANYTHING 

Open Terminal 1:
python udp_server.py

Open Terminal 2:
python udp_client.py

When it asks:
Enter filename to send:
Just type the exact file name:
notes.txt
or
song.mp3

Output file will be created as:
received_notes.txt
received_song.mp3
received_video.mp4
